#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""FBR34KER — authorized ARM64 research and validation toolchain.

Usage:
  ./fbr34ker <command> [options]
  ./fbr34ker menu                   Interactive guided interface

Core commands:
  version              Show version
  doctor               System diagnostics
  build                Build all targets (--security-model, --jobs N)
  test                 Run test suite (--qemu for integration tests)
  run [direct|generic|probe]  Run in QEMU emulation
  clean                Clean build artifacts
  menu                 Interactive goal-driven interface

Device & exploit:
  detect               Auto-detect chipset of connected device
  device               Show connected device info
  pwndfu               Send DWC3 exploit and enter PWNDFU
  load-monitor PATH    Send FBR34KER image via vendor MEM_WRITE
  console              Connect to FBR34KER CDC ACM console
  exploit              Full exploit chain (DWC3 → monitor → jailbreak → boot kernel)

Advanced tools:
  chipsets             List all supported A12+ SoCs
  control-panel        B34ST operator control panel
  b34st [args...]      Run a B34ST command
  b34stool [args...]   B34ST interactive multi-tool
  deploy [args...]     Deploy to device
  module [args...]     Interact with FBR34KER modules
  hardware [args...]   Hardware bring-up workflow
  physical-validation [args...]  Validate physical probe image
  session [args...]    Session management
  package              Create release package
  gate                 Release gate checks
  permissions          Check system permissions
"""
